# The frozen integrity zome.
#
# A circle IS the hash of this compiled wasm. Change the source — including a
# comment, which was measured to change it — and every circle anybody has ever
# made becomes unreachable. Their records stay on their own disks and no build
# of this app will ever show them again, with no error anywhere.
#
# So the hash is pinned here and CI fails if it moves. See the README, and
# docs/to-a-product.md for what to do if it genuinely has to change (short
# answer: that is a migration with everybody re-invited, not a commit).
#
# Rebased 2026-09-09, when the build stopped embedding the building machine's
# home directory. Frozen from the release that follows.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build it with scripts/build-zomes.mjs, never with cargo directly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rust bakes the source path of every dependency into the binary for its panic
# messages. A bare `cargo build` therefore produces a different hash on every
# computer — and the installer released on 2026-09-08 carried the string
# `C:\Users\user\...` inside it. The wrapper passes --remap-path-prefix so that
# any machine of the same platform now produces the same bytes.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows and Linux still differ, and no flag on stable Rust fixes it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The remapped paths keep the operating system's own separator:
#
#   Windows  /cargo\registry\src\...
#   Linux    /cargo/registry/src/...
#
# Different bytes, different DNA, different network. So the two lines below are
# not a reproducibility failure to be fixed — they are a fact about the
# toolchain, and the reason **the released .webhapp is the canonical build**.
# Anybody making a desktop app for another platform assembles it from that
# file rather than compiling the zomes. See the README.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rebased a second time, deliberately. This is a migration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two entry types were added so that the two agreements a circle asks for can
# reach each other inside the circle instead of being carried between devices
# by hand. See docs/to-a-product.md.
#
# **Every circle made before this is unreachable to builds after it.** That is
# not a bug and it is not recoverable: it is what changing this file means, and
# it is why the file is frozen the rest of the time.
#
# The previous hashes, kept so anybody looking at an older build can tell which
# side of the line they are on:
#
#   linux    bc8697a3c80e68b741b9ad6e52cee6ff71e4c9e158b86e69eabec8d82b282d34
#   windows  392dc1703ce4e2a381082784cb9c0169065dd9dff680f90c42679ae0e88b29df
#
# The membrane itself did not change. Whoever joins still presents the same two
# signatures at the door, because somebody who has not joined yet cannot read
# anything inside. What changed is how those two signatures find each other.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rebased a third time, on the same migration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two changes, in one rebase, because the door and the second yes were both
# being rebuilt at once.
#
# One entry type and one link type were added so that being asked to agree to
# who joins is something a person answers rather than something done to them.
# Before this the holder wrote somebody's key into the circle and that was the
# whole of it: they might not know, might not want it, and the first they
# heard was strangers appearing on their screen for approval.
#
# And a knock is now sealed to the holder. With the waiting room the only way
# in, every arrival is announced at a door anybody with the address can read,
# and who visits somebody is itself sensitive. The name and relationship are
# boxed; the key that wrote the knock cannot be hidden and is not.
#
# Still the same migration as the one above -- neither hash has been in a
# release -- so this costs nobody anything beyond what that already cost.
#
#   linux    474f461e0b8c82d5b15a6f65c8a48e5679be862faae664b522ffee66f68716a7
#   windows  6ca5507c96f05c5b39d001117ee1c47386ea7cad33d27bc6e3a6c699c14a068b
#
# The membrane did not change again. What a joiner presents at the door is
# exactly what it was.

linux    24d0090d59f52faf9bd5366f1d6bb5806dd7938338b4c83a6257bed9ef16770d
windows  7700b2092c7691feacde26446807bc9fde791b81a731d6f867c8fe1e2cc1077b
